  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member on iOS 27, I want a « Liquid Glass » icon pack whose drawing is real Icon Composer glass (layered, translucent, specular, shadowed by the system), so that the app icon matches the iOS 27 Home Screen. Operator, 2026-11-27: add the pack with the full-frame H and the faces first; assess which current icons deserve a glass version.\n\n### Prototypes (mac/mac-mbp, 2026-11-27, local only)\nRendered with Xcode's `ictool` (Default, Dark, Clear light/dark, Tinted light/dark). Turning the glass options on a single flat layer changes almost nothing; the glass shows only once the drawing is **split into layers**, each a glass group:\n- **H plein cadre** (from `Icon-CLASSIC.icon`): the white H as one glass group over the yellow-orange gradient.\n- **Face anneau** (from `Icon-REDFACE.icon/Assets/foreground.svg`, ICONS.md §4 rule 2: no deformation): ring and features (eyes + mouth) as two glass groups over the red gradient.\n- **Face disque**: a white glass disc (the face), with the features in red on top, over the red gradient.\n\n### Assessment of the current icons for later glass versions\n| Icon (ICONS.md §2) | Source | Fit for glass | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Défaut `RedFace3D`, REDFACE 3D Big | already layered PNGs (background, eyes, mouth…) | high: the layers exist, glass per layer; it is the default icon | 🟢 next, as « Défaut verre » (keep the 3D art untouched) |\n| REDFACE Blue | SVG (same face) | high: same split as Face anneau, blue fill | 🟢 next |\n| Classique Red | SVG H | high: same split as H plein cadre, red fill | 🟢 next |\n| X-face (plain, Fierté, Dégradé clair/sombre, Or sur noir) | flattened PNGs derived from the face SVG | medium: rebuild as face SVG + background fill layers, then glass; Pride stripes and gradients behind a glass face read well | 🟠 later, 3–5 of the 12 |\n| Beta | SVG | medium: one glyph, check legibility at 29 pt | 🟠 maybe |\n| Classique Blue, Orange, Blue, White, Beta rouge | full-art 1024 px PNG | low: needs a redraw as layers | 🔴 no |\n| Saisons (Noël, Halloween, Printemps, Été, Hiver) | full-art PNG, many details | low: glass blurs small items; dated icons | 🔴 no |\n\n### Scope (this issue)\n- New pack « Liquid Glass » with 3 icons: H plein cadre, Face anneau, Face disque (`Icon-GLASS-H`, `Icon-GLASS-FACE-RING`, `Icon-GLASS-FACE-DISC`, names to confirm), per ICONS.md §5: `.icon` files with Default, Dark and Tinted annotations, `AppIconOption` cases, alternate names in **every** configuration (Debug, Release, Beta), previews via `scripts/icon-previews.sh`, CREDITS, ICONS.md §2 row.\n- No change to the existing icons.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- The three icons appear under « Liquid Glass » in the picker, with previews in light and dark; set as the app icon on a device, they render as glass (screenshots on light and dark Home Screens, Clear and Tinted).\n- Readable at 29 pt; the existing icon tests pass (an option without preview fails).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
